cards.text:
{red|**Before you can rebuild, you need to name what broke.** This is not about rehashing every detail or keeping score. It is about honest acknowledgment of what happened.

If trust was broken by your spouse, what specifically happened?}{red| What did you believe that turned out to be false?}{red| What was the impact on you?}

{red|If you are the one who broke trust, what did you do?}{red| Not the minimized version, but the honest truth of what happened and how it affected your spouse?}

Write an honest account of what happened to break trust in your marriage:

{red|**Take a moment to honestly assess what you are experiencing right now.**

What emotions are most present for you today?}{red| What aspects of the betrayal hurt the most?}{red| What are you grieving?}{red| What do you need that you are not getting?}{red| What fears do you have about the future?}

Write whatever needs to come out:

{red|Based on what happened in your marriage, which components of trust were damaged?}

**Consider reliability, honesty, care, and fidelity.** Some may be severely damaged, some moderately, some may actually be intact.

Write your assessment of which components of trust were damaged and how badly:

{red|What transparency measures would help you feel more secure right now?}

{red|If you are the wounded spouse, what do you need access to?}{red| What would help you feel safer?}{red| Be specific.

If you broke trust, what are you willing to open up?}{red| Are there areas where you feel resistance?}{red| Why might that be?}

Write your transparency needs or offerings:

{red|**Reflect on how questions and disclosure are working in your relationship right now.**

If you are the wounded spouse, what questions do you still have?}{red| Are you getting honest answers?}{red| Do you feel heard when you ask?}

{red|If you broke trust, how are you handling the questions?}{red| Are you being patient and honest?}{red| Where do you feel resistance?}

{red|What would help this dynamic work better for both of you?}

Write your reflection:

{red|**If you broke trust, honestly assess your consistency over the past weeks or months.** Have you been following through on commitments?}{red| Have there been any lies or deceptions?}{red| Where have you been consistent and where have you struggled?}

{red|If your trust was broken, have you noticed any consistent changes in your spouse's behavior?}{red| What would help you recognize and acknowledge the progress that may be happening?}

Write your honest assessment:

{red|**Honestly assess where you are in the forgiveness journey.**

Are you still in the stage of acknowledging the wound and feeling the pain?}

{red|Have you made a choice to forgive, even if you have to keep making it?}

{red|Are there aspects you have forgiven and others you have not?}

{red|What is making forgiveness difficult for you?}

Write where you honestly are:

{red|**Honestly assess where you and your spouse currently stand.**

Do you feel more like adversaries or partners right now?}

{red|What would need to change for you to feel like you are working together instead of against each other?}

{red|What is your role in making that shift happen?}

Write your honest assessment:

{red|**Think about your marriage before the betrayal.** Without excusing what happened, what weaknesses existed in the foundation?}

{red|Were there communication problems?}{red| Emotional distance?}{red| Unaddressed conflict?}{red| Individual issues that were being ignored?}{red| Patterns that were not healthy?}

**This is not about blame.** It is about understanding what needs to be different going forward.

Write your honest assessment of what was weak in the old foundation:

{red|**Together, discuss what you want to build in your new foundation.**

What was missing before that needs to be present now?}

{red|What patterns need to change?}

{red|What practices will you put in place to maintain honesty, intimacy, and health?}

{red|What kind of marriage do you want to create going forward?}

Write your vision for the new foundation of your marriage:

**This vision is not just words on paper.** It is a commitment to build something better than what was broken.

{red|**Think about what living with this scar will look like for your marriage.**

What triggers or difficult dates might you need to navigate together?}

{red|How will you handle the moments when the scar aches?}

{red|What might be the gift in this scar for your future?}

Write your thoughts:

{red|What is the most important thing you have learned through this journey?}

{red|What do you want to remember when the road gets hard?}

{red|What has shifted in how you see your situation, your spouse, or your future?}

Write your greatest insight:

{red|Based on what you have learned, what does your spouse most need from you going forward?}

{red|If you broke trust, what does your spouse need to see from you to continue healing?}

{red|If your trust was broken, what does your spouse need from you to stay engaged in the rebuilding?}

Be specific about what you will give them:
